WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:03.270
Does Ellie believe Joel's big lie?

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.410
Was Ellie prepared to die for the cure?

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:09.550
The last episode of "The Last of Us" Season
1 is as heartbreaking and divisive as the

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:11.198
ending of the game it's based on.

00:00:11.198 --> 00:00:13.399
Warning: spoilers ahead.

00:00:13.508 --> 00:00:17.851
As enigmatic as Joel Miller is, the audience
gets to know a lot about him in the "Last

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.240
of Us" series premiere.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:22.590
Ellie, on the other hand, remains a mystery
for most of Season 1.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:26.410
Vital blanks about her don't get filled in
until the final three episodes.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:31.800
Perhaps the most significant of these open
questions is: Why is Ellie immune to cordyceps?

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:36.660
Viewers are also left wondering about her
parentage, as well as her relationship with Marlene.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.338
"Are you my f---ing mom or something?"

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.252
"Do I look like your mom?"

00:00:41.252 --> 00:00:43.870
"No you do not."

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:49.059
The finale opens with a harrowing pre-title
sequence in which a pregnant woman is running

00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:52.770
for her life through the woods before taking
shelter in an abandoned building.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:57.570
This is Anna, who is in the final stages of
labor when an infected breaches the door and

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:01.680
attacks her just as she's delivering her baby,
whom she names Ellie.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.530
She manages to kill her attacker, but not
before she's bitten in the thigh.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:09.610
To save her child from exposure, she cuts
the umbilical cord with the same knife with

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:11.515
which she dispatched the infected runner.

00:01:11.515 --> 00:01:13.675
Shortly thereafter, Marlene arrives.

00:01:13.675 --> 00:01:18.290
Anna assures her that she was bitten after
the cord was cut, but Marlene is skeptical,

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:19.726
and we know it's a lie.

00:01:19.726 --> 00:01:23.410
It's implied that the exact moment of her
birth rendered Ellie immune.

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:27.869
Marlene promises to care for the baby, before
killing her friend before she turns.

00:01:27.869 --> 00:01:31.930
Presumably, she waits to see if infant Ellie
is showing symptoms before eventually stashing

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:35.470
her with FEDRA where she can keep her safe
and keep tabs on her.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:40.200
When Ellie proves to be resistant to cordyceps,
Marlene and the Fireflies take a renewed interest

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.000
in this miracle child.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.590
Initially, Joel agrees to transport Ellie
out West to a makeshift Firefly hospital in

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:48.750
exchange for some sort of payment.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:53.229
As a bonus, it's his best move for getting
out of the Boston QZ alive and his best hope

00:01:53.229 --> 00:01:54.280
of finding Tommy.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:59.200
But as he and his plucky cargo approach their
final destination, it's painfully obvious

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.939
that Joel no longer cares about his bounty.

00:02:01.939 --> 00:02:05.829
From Ellie's unusually flat affect, we can
deduce that it's only just dawning on her

00:02:05.829 --> 00:02:09.679
and Joel what reaching their goal might mean
– not to mention that she's clearly been

00:02:09.679 --> 00:02:12.610
traumatized from the horrific events of Episode
8.

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:16.970
He floats the idea of forgoing their mission,
suggesting they could instead return to Tommy's

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.980
settlement and try to live as normal a life
as possible.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:24.150
Ellie thanks him for protecting her and says
she'd follow him anywhere, but insists they

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:25.769
keep looking for the hospital.

00:02:25.769 --> 00:02:30.150
Ellie says that after all she's done, she
has to see their journey through to its end.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.687
"It can't be for nothing."

00:02:31.687 --> 00:02:36.590
She tells Joel that there's no going halfway
with their mission, which could mean that

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:39.270
she has realized what might happen to her
if they succeed.

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:41.630
What's weighing on Ellie's conscience is two-fold.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:45.120
To survive, she's killed people and people
have died on her behalf.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.550
Some of those people were innocents and loved
ones.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:51.909
Ellie can't justify her morally compromised
actions if they were only to buy herself some

00:02:51.909 --> 00:02:56.330
more time, even if that time is more meaningful
now that she's partnered up with Joel.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:59.960
She's also working out the math about the
value of her own life versus the value of

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:05.400
a potential cure, which is a heck of an existential
crisis for a teenager in the apocalypse to

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:06.691
have on their shoulders.

00:03:06.877 --> 00:03:11.599
Joel and Ellie don't find the hospital; the
hospital finds them ... or, at least, the

00:03:11.599 --> 00:03:12.881
Fireflies who operate it do.

00:03:12.881 --> 00:03:17.610
After a stun grenade catches them off guard,
Ellie is taken to a reclaimed children's surgery

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:21.600
wing after Joel is knocked out cold with the
butt of a rifle.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.349
When he comes to, Marlene is there to explain
everything.

00:03:24.349 --> 00:03:29.090
The circumstances of Ellie's birth mean that
her body releases chemical signals that tell

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:32.370
cordyceps she's already infected, much like
a vaccine.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:37.176
A doctor affiliated with the Fireflies thinks
he can reproduce that effect with Ellie's cells.

00:03:37.176 --> 00:03:41.610
A devastated Joel figures out that those cells
will have to be harvested from her brain.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:45.760
Marlene acknowledges that she won't survive
the surgery, but she tries to comfort Joel

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:49.819
by assuring him that Ellie will die peacefully
and unaware that she won't wake up from the

00:03:49.819 --> 00:03:51.659
medication she's been given.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.230
"I'm sorry.

00:03:55.032 --> 00:03:57.139
I have no other choice."

00:03:57.139 --> 00:03:58.440
"I do."

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:02.689
In a sequence that mirrors the game, Joel
fights like a demon to rescue Ellie, whom

00:04:02.689 --> 00:04:03.799
he swore to protect.

00:04:03.799 --> 00:04:07.970
Though his main motivation is surely to save
the girl he's come to think of as a second

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:11.959
daughter, he objects to the fact that Ellie
wasn't given a choice in the matter.

00:04:11.959 --> 00:04:15.549
That's his rationale when he's later confronted
by Marlene in the parking garage.

00:04:15.549 --> 00:04:19.769
Since Ellie wasn't told about the procedure
and since she didn't explicitly tell Joel

00:04:19.769 --> 00:04:23.850
she was willing to give her life for a possible
cure – there are, after all, no guarantees

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:28.230
the surgery or experimental treatments would
work – he can't let the Fireflies go through

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:29.230
with their plan.

00:04:29.649 --> 00:04:33.460
For almost all of Season 1 of "The Last of
Us," Joel and Ellie are keeping secrets from

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:34.228
each other.

00:04:34.228 --> 00:04:38.740
She lets him and Tess in on her big secret
— her immunity — pretty quickly, but most

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:42.199
of their emotional baggage stays closed up
until the finale.

00:04:42.199 --> 00:04:45.990
That's when Joel reveals the truth about Sarah
and his gunshot wound and that's when Ellie

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:50.389
finally tells Joel the real story about Riley
and the first time she had to kill.

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:54.930
Eventually, Joel even goes a step further
and begins to openly discuss Sarah again in

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:58.039
a way that he hasn't been able to bring himself
to do since she died.

00:04:58.039 --> 00:05:01.600
Ellie wonders aloud if what he means is that
the passage of time enabled him to better

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:05.670
cope with the loss of Sarah, which means Ellie
may someday be able to better cope with the

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:06.800
loss of Riley.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:09.623
"So time heals all wounds, I guess."

00:05:13.072 --> 00:05:15.000
"It wasn't time that did it."

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.920
It seems like Ellie and Joel both know they
might not see each other again on the other

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.195
side of the Firefly hospital mission.

00:05:21.381 --> 00:05:25.110
Throughout the series, Ellie and Joel make
references to a scar on the right side of

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:28.770
his head and to the fact that his hearing
is diminished in his right ear.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:33.590
The first version of the story he tells Ellie
is simply that someone shot at him and missed.

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:37.740
The audience knows Joel has been through 20
harsh years following the cordyceps outbreak

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:42.199
and the death of his daughter, Sarah, so the
fact that he's worse for the wear isn't surprising

00:05:42.199 --> 00:05:44.330
or particularly noteworthy.

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:47.889
Viewers may have guessed that the wound is
the result of an early shootout with authorities

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:53.960
or an altercation with raiders or other smugglers
at some point in between 2003 and the present.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:58.509
However, in a slight departure from the game,
Joel reveals to Ellie that he's the one who

00:05:58.509 --> 00:05:59.620
shot and missed.

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:02.960
The game merely hints that he's suicidal following
Sarah's death.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:07.370
This moment of extreme honesty and vulnerability
on Joel's part comes as he and Ellie sneak

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:10.419
through a long-defunct military medical encampment.

00:06:10.419 --> 00:06:14.170
Joel remembers how he flinched at the last
second trying to shoot himself the day after

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:15.340
Sarah died.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:19.620
The memory serves to inform us about Joel's
despair on day two of the outbreak as well

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:22.823
as showing us how quickly civilization fell
apart.

00:06:22.823 --> 00:06:26.590
The other mysteries surrounding Ellie have
to do with her friend Riley and the extent

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:28.400
to which Ellie has killed before.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:33.100
In Episode 1, Marlene mentions someone named
Riley, and it strikes a nerve with Ellie,

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:38.819
which is the audience's first clue that something
went awry just prior to the series' main storyline.

00:06:38.819 --> 00:06:42.210
Early on in their journey, Ellie confides
in Joel that she has had to defend herself

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:43.660
with violence before.

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:48.555
To that point, viewers had only seen her put
an infected trapped in a basement out of its misery.

00:06:48.555 --> 00:06:51.569
So when did Ellie have to kill to defend herself?

00:06:51.569 --> 00:06:56.230
The answer is revealed in Episode 7, though
luckily we don't have to watch the horrific

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:57.949
incident play out on screen.

00:06:57.949 --> 00:07:02.020
Riley was Ellie's best friend (and secret
love interest) at the FEDRA school.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:06.690
When Riley was assigned sewage detail as a
FEDRA-designated post-graduate career path,

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:08.780
she defected to the Fireflies.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:13.070
Before she's shipped out on duty to another
QZ, Riley plans a best-night-of-their-lives

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:17.150
at the mall where the two experience some
rare moments of levity and share their true

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:18.683
feelings for each other.

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:24.220
"You're my best friend, and I'll miss you."

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:29.180
Riley intends to say goodbye, but Ellie, who's
less hostile to FEDRA and unsure of how to

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:32.110
feel about the Fireflies, asks her to stay.

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:36.099
Best laid plans rarely work out in "The Last
of Us," and Ellie and Riley are both bitten

00:07:36.099 --> 00:07:38.669
fighting off infected in the Halloween store.

00:07:38.669 --> 00:07:42.639
They decide to live out their final moments
together, but — as Ellie later recounts

00:07:42.639 --> 00:07:45.490
to Joel — this is when she discovers that
she's immune.

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:50.169
Riley succumbs but Ellie doesn't, leaving
Ellie no choice but to kill her crush and

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:51.169
best friend.

00:07:51.258 --> 00:07:55.798
Season 1 of "The Last of Us" ends on a note
that's both heartwarming and unsettling.

00:07:55.798 --> 00:07:59.680
Joel and Ellie look out over the pristine
Wyoming landscape, about to head off into

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:02.400
an uncertain but somewhat hopeful future together.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:06.400
Then, she asks him to swear that everything
he said about the Fireflies was true.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:10.210
Though Joel and Ellie have been hiking for
hours, only moments ago, viewers witnessed

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:11.639
what really happened.

00:08:11.639 --> 00:08:16.110
The Fireflies fully intended to sacrifice
Ellie — the only known person with immunity

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:18.460
— in order to work toward a possible cure.

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:23.580
They attempted to escort Joel out, but Joel
fought back, systematically gunning down Firefly

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:27.430
after Firefly until he reached Ellie unconscious
on her hospital bed.

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:31.510
When Marlene tried to convince him to hand
her over, he shot her with a gun hidden under

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:32.959
Ellie's limp body.

00:08:32.959 --> 00:08:37.659
Of course, that's not the story he tells a
confused Ellie, still in her hospital gown.

00:08:37.659 --> 00:08:40.979
Joel explains that there were dozens like
her and that the Fireflies were merely doing

00:08:40.979 --> 00:08:43.790
some tests to determine if a cure could be
produced.

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:47.130
When their immunity couldn't be replicated,
they gave up on their research.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:51.450
Then, according to Joel, raiders swarmed the
building, and he just barely got her out.

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:54.430
He admits that people died, including Marlene.

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:58.800
Joel swears that his fabricated version is
true, because his new personal mission is

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:00.720
protecting Ellie at all costs.

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:03.960
Ellie's response ends the season, just like
it ended the game.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:10.395
The finale started with Anna lying to Marlene,
and ends with Joel lying to Ellie.

00:09:11.107 --> 00:09:11.819
"Okay."

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:17.330
Is Ellie saying "Okay" her believing the lie,
accepting the lie, or something else?

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:21.880
It's open to interpretation, but fans of "The
Last of Us: Part II" know that their relationship

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:23.180
is forever changed.

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:27.430
Co-creator Craig Mazin, in an episode of the
official "The Last of Us" podcast, said the

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:32.200
ambiguity of the ending is the, quote, "correct"
way to end the story, which is why he kept

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:33.590
it intact from the game.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:35.376
"It can be any of those things."

00:09:35.376 --> 00:09:36.376
"Absolutely."

00:09:36.376 --> 00:09:38.837
"But that's why I love it."

00:09:39.128 --> 00:09:41.269
So what's ahead for Season 2?

00:09:41.269 --> 00:09:45.660
Mazin and showrunner Neil Druckmann aren't
saying much, but they did reveal on the podcast

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:48.750
that fans can expect Season 2 to have a similar
feel.

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:49.750
Druckmann said,

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:53.850
"You can expect us to repeat the same process
[...] The moment-to-moment beats and characters,

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:55.779
they might stay the same, they might change.

00:09:55.779 --> 00:10:00.110
We will do what needs to happen to that story
as it transfers from one medium to another."

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:04.650
And Mazin hinted that Season 1's expansion
into storylines not found in the game, like

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:07.410
the Episode 3 tearjerker, will continue.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:08.410
Mazin said,

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:11.930
"We will also take advantage of the freedom
we have in television that wasn't there in

00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:12.756
the game.

00:10:12.756 --> 00:10:15.577
Specifically, the advantage of changing perspective."

